      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Within the pH range of 5.5 to 7.0, micronutrient availability for grapevines is generally optimized. In this slightly acidic to neutral range, essential metals like iron ($\\text{Fe}$) and manganese ($\\text{Mn}$) remain soluble in the soil solution. As $\\text{pH}$ rises above 7.0, the solubility of both iron and manganese decreases significantly, leading to potential deficiencies in the vines.",
