      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For immediate iron correction, adding chelated iron is the standard recommendation because the chelating agent keeps the iron soluble and mobile even at higher $\\text{pH}$ levels. However, for long-term management, the best approach is often to maintain the soil's $\\text{pH}$ in the optimal range using sulfur amendments. Alternatively, applying acidifying fertilizers or through-stem feeding can help make the existing iron more available to the vines.",
